// A zero divisor is a DEFINED failure, not a panic: `int.div` and `int.mod`
// are total builtins, so the impossible division evaluates to a gradual
// hole, which the machine reports as `Blame::Hole` -- the same discipline
// list-update-out-of-bounds pins for the update ops. The overflowing
// `MIN / -1` blames identically (checked arithmetic, never a wrap).
int.div(1, 0)

// The harness checks:
//@ expect-blame: hole
